-The wrapper accepts `skilled-loop [claude|pi|opencode|codex|cursor|devin] [args...]` and defaults to `claude`. The `cursor` arm launches the `cursor-agent` binary. It keeps the first launch's arguments. Across hops, it preserves model selection for each runtime, the effort flag where the runtime has one (see Model And Effort Across A Hop), the provider flag for Pi, and Pi's extension flags. It resolves relative Pi extension paths against the starting directory before a hop changes directories. It carries `-n` or `--name` for Claude and Pi. The other runtimes have no launch-time name flag. For model, name, Pi extension and Pi provider options, values equal to `--` or starting with `-` stay in the first launch's arguments and are not carried into relaunches.
+The wrapper accepts `skilled-loop [claude|pi|opencode|codex|cursor|devin] [args...]` and defaults to `claude`. The `cursor` arm launches the `cursor-agent` binary. A hop replays the first launch's options in their original order and replaces the start prompt with the claim seed. Model, effort, name, provider and Pi extension settings come from the relaunch record; flags that select or continue a session, including Claude `-c`, `--resume` and `--session-id`, Pi `--session` and `--fork`, OpenCode `--session` and `--prompt`, Codex `--image` and `--worktree`, Devin `--resume` and `--prompt-file`, and Cursor `--worktree` and `--worktree-base`, are in the deny list and are not repeated. Options documented by each runtime's help are replayed with their values, including repeated options. If an unknown option is followed by a bare word, the wrapper warns and declines the hop because it cannot distinguish an option value from the start prompt. Relative Pi extension paths are resolved against the starting directory before a hop changes directories.
 
 The wrapper exports one loop id and starts `SKILLED_LOOP_HOPS` at 0. It relaunches only when a matching record is armed, fresh and below the configured hop limit.
